  "reason": "Evidence: RNA with scgpt improved substantially from singleprofile (0.41) to multiprofile+avgpool (0.53), while image with resnet50 singleprofile is very weak (0.21). We have no data on whether the image modality benefits from multiprofile aggregation. Question: Does multiprofile+avgpool improve the image modality the way it improved RNA? This is a clean single-variable comparison to config_012 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50), directly paralleling the RNA comparison (config_001→config_002). Why this is the best next experiment: The answer determines the strategic direction for all subsequent work—if image improves meaningfully with multiprofile, multimodal fusion becomes a promising avenue to exploit; if it remains near 0.21, the image modality is fundamentally weak with resnet50 and we should prioritize RNA encoder/aggregation improvements or a stronger image encoder instead. This single experiment resolves the largest current uncertainty about whether the image channel carries usable signal, making it the highest-information-use experiment under budget constraints."
}

